# tools/glow_build_concurrency_witness.rish -- two witnesses may build at once, and neither ruins the other.
#
# REDS #88. Every tools/glow_run_worker.sh invocation rebuilt glow/bin/glow_run and wrote glow/.cache, so a
# sweep running beside a hand-run gate wrote the same bytes from two processes at once. The lane that lost
# executed a half-written binary and reported RED about its own logic while nothing was wrong with it, and a
# build killed midway left a truncated glow_run standing for the next entirely clean run to trust. Three false
# REDs in one round were bought this way, and one of them sent a Caravan rung to the ledger that was green.
#
# Two guards close it, in TAME's order of safety before speed: builds serialize behind one bounded lock, and
# every binary is emitted to a private path and moved into place with rename, which is atomic.
#
# This witness proves the guards rather than trusting them. The scan asserts both are still present by marker,
# generates a twin of the real worker with exactly those two stripped, runs both in parallel lanes, and reports
# the difference. The unguarded twin must fail -- a control that survives proves nothing -- and the guarded
# worker must not fail at all, must answer on every lane, and must leave no temporary behind.
#
# Kin: tools/fixtures/glow_build_concurrency_scan.sh (the experiment), tools/glow_run_worker.sh (the guards),
# tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish and tools/glow_tend_a1_suite.rish (the two choirs that raced).
#
# This authors no build -- it runs and compares. Purely local: no key, no signature, no network, no funds, no device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/glow_build_concurrency_witness.rish

say "glow-build-concurrency: Language EN -- two witnesses may build at once, and neither ruins the other."
say "glow-build-concurrency: Style Radiant -- the guard is measured against a control generated from the very worker it guards, so the proof can never drift away from the code."
say "glow-build-concurrency: Lens TAME -- safety before speed: one bounded lock, one atomic rename. RED names which half gave way. Purely local -- no key, no network, no funds, no device."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/glow_build_concurrency_scan.sh"]
assert scan.ok else "glow-build-concurrency: the concurrency scan failed to run -- ${scan.err}"
say scan.out

# The guards are still in the worker. Checked first, so a passing run can never mean
# "measured a worker that quietly lost them."
assert scan.out contains "CONC_GUARDS_PRESENT 2" else "glow-build-concurrency: the worker no longer carries both guards -- the lock and the atomic install"

# The control must fail. A control that survives its own hazard proves nothing at all.
assert ((scan.out contains "CONC_UNGUARDED_FAILS 0") == false) else "glow-build-concurrency: the unguarded twin survived every lane -- the RED path is unproven, so the guard is unmeasured"

# The guarded worker must come home clean on every lane, and leave nothing half-built.
assert scan.out contains "CONC_GUARDED_FAILS 0" else "glow-build-concurrency: the guarded worker failed a lane -- serialization is not holding"
assert scan.out contains "CONC_GUARDED_ANSWERED 6" else "glow-build-concurrency: a guarded lane did not answer EXIT:0"
assert scan.out contains "CONC_LEFTOVER_TEMPS 0" else "glow-build-concurrency: a half-built temporary was left behind -- an interrupted build must leave the previous good binary standing"

assert scan.out contains "CONC_OK" else "glow-build-concurrency: the scan reported CONC_BAD -- read the line above for which half gave way"
assert ((scan.out contains "CONC_BAD") == false) else "glow-build-concurrency: CONC_BAD present"

say "GREEN: glow-build-concurrency -- six lanes at once; the unguarded twin falls, the guarded worker answers on every lane and leaves nothing half-built (REDS #88 prevention on metal)."
